From d28a3f11c7373affb0100b9469e9fbee28248620 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: build <build@localhost>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 09:32:36 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] Hide identity disc and stale Google options

This build has no Play services, no Google account sign-in, and metrics/UKM
upload compiled out, so the following surfaces only promise things that can
never work. Remove them:

- NTP identity disc ("Signed out. Opens options to sign in." toolbar button):
  IdentityDiscController never marks its ButtonData showable, so the optional
  toolbar slot falls through to the adaptive toolbar button, the same as
  upstream's SigninLevelUpButton configuration. Sign-in does nothing without
  Play services.
- Settings > Google services:
  - "Allow Chrome sign-in": there is no sign-in to allow.
  - "Help improve features and performance" (usage_and_crash_reports):
    metrics upload is compiled out.
  - "Make searches and browsing better" (url_keyed_anonymized_data): UKM is
    compiled out.
  - Price tracking annotations and price notifications: Google Shopping
    backend, not used.
  Kept: "Improve search suggestions" (talks to the chosen search engine),
  "Usage stats reporting" (Android Digital Wellbeing, device-local) and
  Touch to Search. The PREF_* keys referenced by tests stay.
- Settings main page sign-in row (SignInPreference, "sign_in"): its "Sign in
  to ..." promo can never complete. Removed from main_preferences.xml, the
  MainSettings wiring (ProfileDataCache, bottom-sheet sign-in coordinator)
  and the search-index entry. ManageSyncSettings was only reachable through
  that row; its index entries are now orphaned and pruned by resolveIndex.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
